<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
		Entitlement baseline for PERSONAL USE (no Apple Developer account, ad-hoc signing).

		History / why this file is now minimal:
		  - Originally it carried `get-task-allow` (debugger attach) and
		    `keychain-access-groups = [$(AppIdentifierPrefix)$(CFBundleIdentifier)]`.
		  - Both require signing with a DEVELOPMENT certificate. This client is built with
		    ad-hoc identity (CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = "-"), and this host has zero codesigning
		    identities, so those entitlements made the Catalyst build fail with
		    "Mattermost has entitlements that require signing with a development certificate."
		  - T20 decision: a fully empty entitlements dict is the correct content for a
		    personal, locally-run ad-hoc Catalyst/iOS build. No App Sandbox entitlement is
		    applied (ENABLE_APP_SANDBOX = NO in the pbxproj) because there is no App Store
		    review to satisfy and the sandbox would block file/network access for a locally-run
		    build; we disable it deliberately (documented in docs/t20-build-note.md).
		    `get-task-allow` is dropped because it is a development-certificate entitlement and
		    is meaningless under ad-hoc signing (simulator builds do not need it). On a physical
		    device you would debug via the normal Xcode development-signing flow, which supplies
		    its own entitlements.

		Credentials note: SecureVault stores per-server auth tokens as kSecClassGenericPassword
		items scoped by kSecAttrService (server canonical URL) + kSecAttrAccount (secret name).
		That API does NOT require a keychain-access-groups entitlement - access groups are only
		for SHARING items across app groups/targets. This app is a single target; the only
		future keychain-sharing consumer (the push NotificationServiceExtension) is blocked as
		publishing-only (T12/T13); re-add keychain-access-groups when that extension lands and
		is signed with a development/provisioning identity.
	-->
</dict>
</plist>